WEBVTT

00:00:01.880 --> 00:00:05.460
This is the Microsoft for Education Daily, for Tuesday.

00:00:06.560 --> 00:00:09.510
Let's catch you up on everything new from Microsoft.

00:00:15.000 --> 00:00:15.890
Press start.

00:00:15.890 --> 00:00:21.540
Every Durham University student now has Microsoft 365 Copilot, reports say.

00:00:22.500 --> 00:00:27.620
Phase one puts Copilot in Word, Outlook and Excel, on existing accounts.

00:00:31.880 --> 00:00:35.380
Where assessment rules allow, students can summarise notes,

00:00:35.380 --> 00:00:38.470
plan towards deadlines and structure presentations.

00:00:39.380 --> 00:00:43.130
Durham says Copilot only sees what students could already see,

00:00:43.130 --> 00:00:45.190
and their entries won't train AI.

00:00:46.880 --> 00:00:50.360
And the university's line for students: your thinking,

00:00:50.360 --> 00:00:53.400
knowledge, expertise and judgement come first.

00:00:53.910 --> 00:00:54.570
In Kuwait,

00:00:54.570 --> 00:00:59.520
a new Microsoft innovation centre plans AI workshops and student programs.

00:01:00.000 --> 00:01:04.980
In preview, school IT can lock a lost or stolen Windows laptop from Intune,

00:01:04.980 --> 00:01:06.240
without wiping it.

00:01:07.500 --> 00:01:10.010
Everyone's signed out, sign-in disappears,

00:01:10.010 --> 00:01:13.060
and the lock holds through restarts, even offline.

00:01:15.000 --> 00:01:18.380
Works on Windows Education, Pro or Enterprise.

00:01:18.380 --> 00:01:22.120
Keep BitLocker on, though: USB boot isn't blocked.

00:01:22.500 --> 00:01:24.370
For university code teams,

00:01:24.370 --> 00:01:28.470
GitHub can now start AI Scans on up to 20 repos at once.

00:01:30.000 --> 00:01:30.700
In the lab,

00:01:30.700 --> 00:01:36.200
UC Berkeley and Microsoft built an open-source plugin that helps coding agents learn.

00:01:37.500 --> 00:01:43.170
On 277 real bug fixes, it cut costs 18 to 31%.

00:01:45.000 --> 00:01:50.790
The fine print? Windows Server 2016 gets its last security update in January.

00:01:52.500 --> 00:01:55.770
After that, it's Extended Security Updates only,

00:01:55.770 --> 00:01:58.020
so plan the move to Server 2025.

00:02:01.880 --> 00:02:06.910
After hours, Xbox brought back its original boot-up animation,

00:02:06.910 --> 00:02:09.260
for Series X|S and Xbox One.

00:02:09.380 --> 00:02:15.680
Two Xbox 360 boot screens came back too, free, for Xbox's 25th birthday.

00:02:16.880 --> 00:02:22.620
And Minecraft Dungeons II's DLC, The Humblers Awaken, arrives December 1.

00:02:23.910 --> 00:02:28.850
Whatever you're starting this week, a course, a rollout or a game: press start.

00:02:30.000 --> 00:02:33.020
Day after day, the updates keep stacking up.

00:02:33.750 --> 00:02:36.800
Check the board: shipped today, and more on the way.

00:02:37.500 --> 00:02:40.690
All of that, in one day. And it keeps on shipping.

00:02:45.000 --> 00:02:47.720
This has been the Microsoft for Education Daily.

00:02:48.750 --> 00:02:51.340
Go build something. See you tomorrow.
